WEBVTT

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.040
<b>First Shrine Visit</b>

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.540
First shrine visit!

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.330
Happy New Year!

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.290
Same to you!

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.290
Nishikata!

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:15.540
Takagi-san...

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.250
Happy New Year to you.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.080
Happy New Year...

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:30.920
They're really warm.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.250
These gloves that you gave me for Christmas.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.630
Oh, uh, that's good.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.210
This scarf you gave me is really warm, too.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.130
You came by yourself?

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.040
No, with my family.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.250
They ran into some old friends and
got caught up in conversation.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.210
Oh yeah? Same here.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:56.250
Hey. Let's go visit the shrine together.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.250
Sure. Whatever.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.170
Hooray!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.290
It's pretty crowded.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.420
Well, it is January 1st.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:20.290
I know it's not surprising, but there are
mostly only families or couples here today.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.500
We don't really fit in either category,
so it's kind of weird, huh?

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.790
Uh, so we're supposed to do
2 bows, 2 claps, then 1 bow, right?

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.420
Yeah, that sounds right.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.290
My wish for this year is that
I don't get teased by Takagi-san!

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.420
What did you wish for?

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:46.000
Not saying. It's private.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.460
Maybe something about
not getting teased by me this year?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.710
I knew it!

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.080
Crap! She's already doing it!

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:57.670
Why?!

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.290
What did you wish for, Takagi-san?

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:04.500
It's a secret.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:05.830
Try guessing.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.330
I bet you just wished for more opportunities
to tease me or whatever.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.420
Nope.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.750
Because I already know that'll happen
even if I don't wish for it.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.880
Curse you, Takagi-san!

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:20.960
Hey, Nishikata.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.540
Let's have our first contest of the new year.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.130
What?

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.330
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:31.210
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:31.210
<b>100 YEN</b>

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.830
We'll both pull our own fortunes.
And whoever has the luckier one wins.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:35.130
Interesting. That means the winner
is entirely based on luck.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.540
The year has barely started and I'm already getting
teased, so I'll use this opportunity to change that!

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.500
I accept your challenge, Takagi-san.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.000
You can go first.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.670
She's not even worried.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:53.250
Just watch, I'm gonna beat you for sure
by pulling the best fortune there is!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.920
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.920
<b>100 YEN</b>

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.080
That was fast!

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.380
Please! Say "amazing luck"!

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.380
<b>Fortune</b>

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.750
<b>Plain Luck</b>

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.000
Oh!

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.080
Is "plain" considered good?

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.580
If I remember right, it's the one after "amazing luck".

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.420
I think it's better than "some luck" and "little luck".

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.920
Wow! Then so long as Takagi-san
doesn't pull "amazing luck",

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.920
this contest will end up a draw at worst!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.670
<b>Amazing Luck</b>

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.460
You gotta be kidding!

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:26.830
<b>AMAZAKE</b>

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:26.830
<b>200 YEN</b>

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.960
I'd like 2 servings, please.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.920
Comin' right up! That'll be 400 yen, please.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.170
This is yummy, huh?

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:37.880
Yeah.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.210
Was it a wish for good health?

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.000
Oh. You mean what I wished for earlier?

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:48.920
Wrong.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.170
Dang it! I'm already doing nothing but losing this year.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:56.630
I have to hurry and guess this right, no matter what!

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.710
Oh, it's my mom.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:05.380
Yeah? I'm having some amazake now.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.250
Okay. Sure.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.420
Sounds good. Yeah.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:14.130
Sorry. I have to go meet with my family.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.040
Wait!

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:22.210
What? You wanted to hang out with me a little longer?

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.380
Uh, no, that's not exactly...

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.170
I'm just kidding.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.710
It feels good since I won our first contest of the year.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:34.170
I'm glad we ran into each other.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.710
Well, when we do it again next year,
I'm gonna get the better fortune!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:46.210
So, in other words, you're inviting me
to join you for next year's first shrine visit?

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.630
Uh... er... well...

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.830
O-only if we run into each other again...

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.830
I really hope we get to do it again next year.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:56.710
Just like today.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.420
Uh... sure. Let's do it next year.

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:05.170
I know my parents are gonna be busy
talking to their friends again, anyway.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:09.040
Well, that was fast. My wish already came true.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:09.830
Huh?

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:14.880
What I wished for earlier was that you would
ask me out on a date again, Nishikata.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:15.920
Wha?!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.040
W-wait, that's not...

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.250
I wasn't asking you out on a date!

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.630
And I know you're totally lying about your wish!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.330
Here's to another year of fun together!

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.830
Darn you, Takagi-san!

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.380
<b>Snowman</b>

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:31.630
Snowman!

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:42.130
Awesome! It snowed! It snowed a bunch!

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.420
Yahoo!

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.830
<b>You have a new message</b>

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.580
Yo, Takagi-san!

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.460
Oh! Nishikata!

00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.540
You got here fast.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.080
Must be because of how excited
you are about all the snow, huh?

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.500
N-not really. Nothing exciting about it.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:10.210
But it's uncommon to get this
much snow around here, you know.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:15.210
Yeah, totally! I think it's been like 5 years since
the last time! It almost never piles up like this!

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.670
Uh, not that I'm excited about it or anything...

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:26.080
Anyway, let's hurry and get started! You're the one
who proposed we have a snowman contest!

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.080
<b>Wanna have a snowman contest</b>

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.080
<b>over at the empty lot?</b>

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.080
<b>Okay</b>

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.460
That's right. Let's do it.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:31.250
Okay, come over this way.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:39.170
I wore these gloves today since
the snow will get them all wet.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.130
Oh yeah?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:50.000
A pair of thick gloves, huh? I bet she thinks that will give
her the upper hand here, but boy is she wrong!

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:55.250
Because little does she know, I'm a total pro
when it comes to making big snowmen!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:59.380
Although, I haven't made one
since I was in elementary school.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.630
The time limit is 30 minutes.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:04.580
And we can't use any tools, okay?

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:08.000
That's it. Whoever can make
the better snowman is the winner.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.880
Okay. I'm ready to start.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.750
Huh? Did you say a "better snowman"?!

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.290
Not a "bigger snowman"?!

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.130
It's the better snowman.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.710
A-and just how the heck are we gonna judge that?!

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.330
Let's decide by giving each other a score.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.750
I'm screwed!

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.380
I totally thought this was going to be a size contest!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.250
What does a good snowman even look like?!

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:37.380
Well, I don't mind if we make size part of the points.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.460
It's only fair, since I forgot to explain the details.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:42.710
She definitely didn't tell me on purpose.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.040
Ready?

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.250
Start!

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.750
Artistic points and size points.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.330
Whoever gets the most overall will win, huh?

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.170
Fine then.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:57.960
All I have to do is focus on making mine extra big!

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.500
Oh?

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:05.170
Well, I'm going to fetch some decorations first.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:07.210
You think it's so easy, don't you, Takagi-san?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.580
But you've only got 30 minutes!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:15.830
All right, let's build this up. I gotta make sure the
core is extra firm as I pack more snow over it...

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:25.460
Okay, this is perfect! I'm gonna make it even bigger!

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:29.170
Wow! That's huge!

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:33.040
She's obviously freaked out.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:36.710
Because she definitely didn't expect me
to make mine this big!

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:41.040
And I'm not done yet, this is just the beginning!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:47.630
It's done!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.880
This one is gonna be the body.
And next I'm gonna make the head!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.880
Let's see, how is Takagi-san doing?

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:59.380
Whoa, that looks...

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:01.630
like a really good snowman!

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:04.580
It's gonna be fun deciding your penalty after I win.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.080
Fine! I'll just make mine even bigger!

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:27.080
SUPER MOVE! ROLLING SNOOOOOOOW!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.290
One minute left.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:34.250
Check these bad boys out!

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.460
They got a little dirty from all the rolling,

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:42.040
but they're so huge I'm definitely gonna beat
Takagi-san puny snowman!

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:47.750
30 seconds left.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:51.540
Wh-whatever! I just gotta finish...

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.580
Dang it!

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.250
It's too heavy!

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:58.920
I should have known! It was already
hard enough just for me to push it!

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.040
I'm so stupid!

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.000
15 seconds left.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.500
Screw it! I've gotta get this done!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.130
<b>Start</b>

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.130
<b>Reset</b>

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:31.380
Looks like I'm the winner.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.960
Since you didn't finish your snowman in time, Nishikata.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:42.210
It feels like I would've lost even if I had finished it...

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:45.420
Okay. Let me help you with that.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.040
Huh?

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:49.080
Nah, that's okay. It's too heavy.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.040
Besides, I already lost...

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.750
You went to all that trouble, so let's finish it!

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.830
Yay! It's all done!

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:04.830
I knew it...

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.790
I was doomed to lose either way.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.130
Well, should we head home?

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.330
Uh... yeah.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.920
Almost like a married couple, huh?

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:22.750
What?!

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.460
Our snowmen, I mean.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:30.210
Uh, no, they look more like parent and child to me...

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.000
Hey, Nishikata.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:33.670
Huh?

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.330
Treat me to a warm drink, would you?

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:36.880
And not because you lost or anything.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.380
Huh?! Then why should I?!

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:46.080
<b>New Years</b>

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.000
New Years!

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:48.710
Yo, Kimura!

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.920
You're commanding a more
powerful presence than usual.

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:57.420
You noticed? Let's just say that I transcended
a new gateway during the holidays.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.670
A new gateway?

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.000
For breakfast,

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.830
I managed to eat 30 servings of mochi!

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:06.880
That's called overeating, dude.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.250
Happy New Year!

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:10.540
Happy New Year.

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.290
Happy New Year.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:16.000
I hope that we all can enjoy another good year together.

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:19.540
This feels kinda silly.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:23.750
We already wrote that stuff on the cards we sent,
so why bother with all the formalities?

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.290
It's important to stay on good terms, you guys!

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:29.630
C'mon, don't you know how that old nursery rhyme goes?

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:35.040
One for the money, two for the show, three friends
gotta stick together or to the four winds they go!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.210
The heck is that?

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:41.170
It's a brand new year! So we gotta start it right!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:44.080
Why did the new year holiday have to end, anyway?

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:46.460
I really wish it was longer!

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.880
Yeah, I feel you.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.080
So, what did you guys do during the holiday?

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:53.920
A ton of stuff!

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.790
I went kite flying,

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:57.540
played karuta,

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.580
played board games,

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.790
and had a ton of fun hanging with my relatives!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:02.830
That's what elementary kids do.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.750
Well, I'm a middle schooler!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:05.830
Oh, right.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.580
How did you spend your vacation, Sanae?

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.960
I pretty much spent the entire time running.

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:12.170
Whoa.

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.960
You sure love track and field, huh?

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:17.330
I ran to visit all of my relatives and collect
the new year gift money they owed me.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:18.210
Huh?

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:22.170
I was able to buy some new shoes with it all.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:23.710
Wow.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:25.380
What did you do, Yukari?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:26.920
Uh...

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.250
Well, just some stuff.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:32.670
You lazed around in bed the whole time, huh?

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.630
Busted!

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:38.000
What's wrong with that?!
We're all free to do whatever we want!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.000
That's so you!

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:45.830
Hi, Nishikata-kun.

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:48.790
Got a minute?

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:51.000
Um... yeah.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:55.750
<b>Advice</b>

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:57.540
Sorry to bother you.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:59.130
Uh, it's cool.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.000
So, what's up?

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:06.080
Well... I'd like to ask you a question.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.290
What is something you want?

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:09.500
Huh?

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:12.630
Oh, I'm sorry. I should've explained first.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:15.000
Let's see...

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:17.880
You know Hamaguchi, right?

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:19.460
It's about him...

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.580
I'm wondering what sort of thing he would like.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.790
You know, since his birthday is coming up soon.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.670
Oh, I see...

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:30.290
Hold on! Please don't get the wrong idea.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:34.830
He's the one who gave me a gift first, you know. I'm not
giving him anything, just returning the favor and that's it.

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.080
You get me?

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.290
Uh, y-yeah.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:41.880
Good.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.500
Now we're clear.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:47.960
So any ideas?

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:50.290
About what he might want?

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:52.790
You two are close friends, aren't you?

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:56.170
Well, um...

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.330
This is just what I heard from the girls in class,

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.750
but apparently Hojo has gotten
hooked on baking cookies lately.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.330
She's always been bad at cooking, though.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:09.920
Still, Hojo's cookies might be good.
I really wanna try them for myself!

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:12.670
Uh...

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.630
He mentioned that he wanted to try eating
your homemade cookies, I think.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:21.420
Huh?! H-how on earth does he know that
I started baking cookies as a hobby?!

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.330
S-sorry, I've got no idea.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:28.290
Well, that helps. So he wants to eat
my homemade cookies? How sweet...

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:35.170
Great. I didn't want to spend money on him anyway.

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:37.710
Cookies are a cheap gift. Fitting for Hamaguchi.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.920
Thanks. I appreciate your help.

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.830
Uh, sure.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.250
Oh, right.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.750
Keep this conversation just between you and me, okay?

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:48.790
Will do...

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.040
Can I come over and play games at your place?

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:51.790
Sure.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:01.170
By the way, Nishikata.

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:04.080
Did you talk with Hojo-san during lunch break today?

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:04.710
Huh?!

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:05.920
How do you know that?

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:07.920
Because I saw you two.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:09.790
What were you talking about?

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.420
Oh, well, she was asking...

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:14.710
Just between you and me, okay?

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:18.880
Well, it was about nothing, really.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:20.250
Oh?

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:21.960
You mean it was something secret?

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.210
Yeah, you could say that.

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:29.960
I bet she was curious to know
what Hamaguchi wants for a gift.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.670
Uh, what makes you think that?

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.210
My intuition.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.290
Was I right?

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.290
I swear, it's like she can read minds or something!

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:43.210
But I have to keep it secret...

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:46.540
Dunno.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.210
Oh?

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:10.750
Hey.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:16.000
Is there something you would like
to get for a present, Nishikata?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:19.670
Look, I'm telling you, I didn't
talk about that with Hojo-san...

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:22.250
It has nothing to do with that, I'm just curious.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.250
It would help me decide on what to get someone.

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:31.790
A present for someone? Who exactly?

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.830
A 15-year-old boy. Maybe.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.540
Someone... a year older than me?

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:48.080
No, forget it. Tough luck, Takagi-san!
You won't fool me this time!

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.170
It's just gonna be some dog again!

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:53.420
I thought that chihuahua was 16 years old?

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.170
Huh?

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:58.290
No, not a dog. I'm talking about
a 3rd year middle schooler.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.250
Huh?

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:03.920
Weird. I thought for sure that
was another set up to tease me.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.080
Well, uh...

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:08.790
I don't know.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:13.330
C'mon, put a little more thought into it than that.

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:16.170
Nah, I'm not...

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:18.130
Because I'm talking about you!

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:22.330
What?

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:28.330
It's the present I'm going
to give you on your next birthday.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.130
Um... er...

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.380
Tell me when you think of something.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.420
S-sure.

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:43.960
For some reason... I feel a little relieved...

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:51.040
So... hey.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:53.880
Sorry.

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:58.250
I wish I could tell you what Hojo-san
and I talked about, but I can't.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:01.920
Because I promised I wouldn't.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.330
I'm sorry, too.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.830
I feel like... I did something mean.

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:25.330
Hold up. Don't you always?

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:26.670
Huh?

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.080
What I always do is just playful teasing.

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:31.790
Huh...?

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:34.540
Okay...

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.130
But... why though?

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.210
Who knows?

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:57.920
These are so warm.

00:21:58.630 --> 00:22:00.630
The present you gave me.
